For a controlled variation, change \verb|count: .long 42| to \verb|count: .long 41|, reassemble \texttt{value.o}, and relink. The displacement, relocation kinds, and segment sizes should stay the same; the first four bytes of the writable segment change from \texttt{2a 00 00 00} to \texttt{29 00 00 00}, and the shell should report \(41\). This separates the payload supplied by the assembler from the layout chosen by the linker and the initialization performed by the loader.
